00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:28.480
Then they dug a hole?

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:33.490
Wolf's Neck

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:33.490
South Fort

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:33.490
North Fort

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.940
That's even more absurd!

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:37.280
Then they came through Wolf's Neck?

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:48.710
Well, what did you think? That they'd come strolling through the Wolf's Neck and tell the guard,

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:55.010
Wolf's Neck

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:55.010
South Fort

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:55.010
North Fort

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:55.550
"Step aside, friend, we're planning to move into the North Fort this very night!"

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:59.010
or something like that?

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:02.560
Then if you know so much about it,

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.730
which way did they come?

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.770
Well...

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:11.070
Not through the Wolf's Neck and the big fortress gate, by all accounts.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:13.490
They came from the north side, of course.

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:19.030
Wolf's Neck

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:19.030
South Fort

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:19.030
North Fort

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:17.320
We don't have any guards on the north side.

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:23.580
Why should we keep a guard there?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:28.190
There's no entrance to the fort, and just a sheer rock wall besides.

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:35.130
Do you think they're like flies who can climb straight up into the air?

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:43.470
That aside,

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:47.060
what were you doing up on the roof?

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:52.310
I was being careful not to fall into Hell's Gap.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:07.580
<i>How'd the Borka robbers get into the north fort?</i>

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:10.250
<i>I should've asked Birk.</i>

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:20.600
Ronja, go to sleep now.

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:21.430
Yup.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:31.060
From now on, we're watching over the rooftop as well.

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:34.610
Sturkas, Tjegge, Lill-Klippen.

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:36.700
Yes, boss.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.240
Leave it to us.

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:39.610
We'll watch 'em for sure.

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:43.410
Borka's nerve is just too much.

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:46.620
At any moment he'll come rushing over Hell's Gap like a wild bull,

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:50.700
and drive us out of the fort.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.920
I'm going to bed!

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:03.040
Not to sleep, but to think, and to curse!

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:07.890
And woe betide anyone who disturbs me!

00:22:39.930 --> 00:22:41.050
Hey!

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:43.070
Robber's daughter!

00:22:43.070 --> 00:22:44.940
I'll be seeing you!

00:22:49.390 --> 00:22:52.670
She had met someone of her own age, at last,

00:22:52.670 --> 00:22:58.770
but why did it have to be a nasty little Borka robber?

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:03.830
Ronja couldn't fall asleep very fast that night.

